From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chad Cormier Roussel <chadcormierroussel@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 16:20:20 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] mtld3d: the D3D9 M2b review's minors: tests executed per
 subtest, every lint suppression audited

The conformance runner prints each subtest's executed tests (Wine's
summary lines summed), so a run that stopped early without crashing is
told from an improvement. make audit sees module-level #![allow(...)]
too, and CONVENTIONS lists every one, the facade's objc2-shaped class
among them. The facade's commit lock lives in commit(), and its VM
comment names the real hazard: a queue runs its buffers in the order
the host commits them, while a wait blocks for a later commit anyway.
Two comments corrected (no Linux crash reporter; nothing at load may
call winemetal).

Assisted-by: Claude Code: claude-opus-5-5
